# Secret environment for the basic-delivery example.
#
# Copy to secrets/.env (gitignored) to provide the coding agent's LLM provider
# credentials and any local machine-specific overrides. run.sh sources this file
# and exports its variables into the single `temper run` process, so whatever the
# selected provider (TEMPER_RUN_AUTH in config/temper.env) needs must be set here.
#
# Forgejo role tokens/passwords are minted by run.sh into secrets/credentials.toml
# (gitignored, 0600) — the runtime's own credentials format, loaded via
# `temper daemon --credentials`; they are NOT pasted here.
#
# --- Coding-agent provider auth ----------------------------------------------
# DeepSeek (TEMPER_RUN_AUTH=deepseek): set the API key directly.
# TEMPER_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# ChatGPT / Anthropic OAuth (TEMPER_RUN_AUTH=chatgpt-oauth|anthropic-oauth):
# these read their own OAuth auth file rather than a bare key. Point the run at it
# by adding `--auth-file <path>` (e.g. via a TEMPER_RUN_BIN wrapper) or by
# completing the provider's documented OAuth login so the default auth file
# exists.
#
# --- Local binary overrides (optional) ---------------------------------------
# TEMPER_FORGEJO_BINARY=/absolute/path/to/forgejo-7.0.12-linux-amd64
# TEMPER_FORGEJO_RUNNER_BINARY=/absolute/path/to/forgejo-runner-3.5.1-linux-amd64
# TEMPER_RUN_BIN=/absolute/path/to/temper
